sc("crit154", "Criticisms of 802.15.4", "Slide 19 · Criticisms", "Criticisms of IEEE 802.15.4",
   cards([("🎲","MAC reliability & latency","Uses **CSMA/CA** for media access. Collision handling and **random wait times** can cause **unbounded latency** and **reliability issues**.","c7",0),
          ("📻","Interference & multipath fading","**No frequency hopping** → more easily hit by **interference** and **multipath** signal degradation.","c6",3),
          ("🛠️","Fixed in later variants","**802.15.4e** and **802.15.4g** improve MAC reliability, latency and interference → more robust for more applications.","c5",5)], cols=3),
   ["It has criticisms too. First, MAC reliability and latency. It uses CSMA/CA, carrier sense multiple access with collision avoidance, to share the channel.",
    "Because devices wait random times after collisions, delay has no upper limit. That's called unbounded latency.",
    "This also leads to reliability issues.",
    "Second, interference and multipath fading. It lacks frequency hopping, so it is more sensitive to interference.",
    "Multipath means the signal bounces off walls and arrives several times, weakening itself.",
    "The later standards, IEEE 802.15.4e and 802.15.4g, add enhancements to fix MAC reliability, latency and interference, making it more robust."],
   tip=("Criticism: **CSMA/CA → unbounded latency** + **no frequency hopping**. Fix: **15.4e / 15.4g**.", 0))

